Overview: Investigated a site availability outage for yummyrecipesforme.com by capturing and analyzing live packet data using tcpdump. Isolated the issue to network-layer communication failures during DNS resolution.
Technical Incident Summary: Symptom: Users reported destination unreachable browser errors when attempting to access the web application.  Traffic Analysis Findings:Client machine (192.51.100.15) initiated standard UDP lookup queries to Port 53 for domain name resolution.  Instead of an IP resolution response, the system captured inbound ICMP error packets originating from 203.0.113.2 explicitly stating that UDP Port 53 was unreachable.  Scope Isolation: Confirmed the outage was isolated to the name resolution service (DNS) rather than a failure of the web application server itself. 
Root Cause & Vulnerability Analysis: Identified three primary potential root causes for the Port 53 failure:  Firewall / Security Group Misconfiguration: Network access control rules inadvertently blocking inbound UDP traffic on Port 53.  DNS Daemon Failure: Service crash or unconfigured DNS daemon on the target host.  Denial of Service (DoS): Volumetric malicious traffic exhausting DNS server resources and dropping legitimate queries.
Tools & Methodologies Used: tcpdump, Packet Inspection, ICMP Protocol Analysis, DNS Lookup Resolution (UDP Port 53), Root Cause Diagnostics.
